+# RELIABILITY_DRILLS
+
+Version-controlled record of the operational reliability controls and the
+per-release exercise of them. This closes the documentation half of
+`FINAL-P2-001` (reliability controls not versioned or exercised per release):
+the recovery point/objective and the drill procedure are now committed, and
+each release candidate must capture the drill evidence below. Runtime code and
+the host schedule are unchanged.
+
+## Recovery objectives (RPO / RTO)
+
+| Objective | Target | Basis |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| **RPO** | ≤ 24 h | Daily `pg_dump -Fc` at 04:00 UTC, tiered S3 (DO Spaces) rotation; worst-case loss is the gap since the last verified dump. |
+| **RTO** | ≤ 4 h | Restore into a scratch project, validate, then switch production (see [BACKUP_RESTORE.md](BACKUP_RESTORE.md)). |
+
+These are the operator targets for the certified single-host stack. They are
+**targets, not measurements**: a target becomes evidence-backed only when a
+drill (below) records the observed restore time and recovery point. Until then,
+treat the last verified daily dump as the recovery point (`≤24h`).
+
+## Version-controlled controls
+
+The controls referenced by `FINAL-P2-001`/`OBS-P1-001`, with the in-repo
+artifact that carries them:
+
+| Control | Cadence / rule | In-repo source |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Database backup | daily 04:00 UTC; S3 tiered (Sun full 365d, daily 30d) | [BACKUP_RESTORE.md](BACKUP_RESTORE.md) |
+| Assurance quick lane | `*/5 * * * *`; container health, cert < 14d, disk < 2 GB alert | [ASSURANCE.md](ASSURANCE.md), `scripts/assurance/assurance.sh` |
+| Assurance daily lane | `17 5 * * *`; tests, backup freshness, exception drift, scans | [ASSURANCE.md](ASSURANCE.md) |
+| Alert delivery | any non-zero lane exit → ntfy (`NTFY_TOPIC`, host-only) | [INCIDENT.md](INCIDENT.md) |
+| Recovery reconciliation | per run; atomic, idempotent | `evidence/recovery/README.md` |
+| Image rollback | per deploy; retag `:previous` → `:certified` | [ROLLBACK.md](ROLLBACK.md) |
+
+The crontab schedule itself still lives only on the host — that remains
+`OBS-P1-001` (see [INCIDENT.md](INCIDENT.md#known-gaps)). This runbook makes
+the schedule and thresholds reviewable in-repo; committing the crontab/timer
+file is the follow-up for that P1.
+
+## Per-release drills
+
+Run these for every release candidate; if no release is cut for 30 days, run
+them at least monthly for bounded runtime use. A drill that is not captured as
+evidence did not happen.
+
+1. **Backup/restore drill** — restore the newest dump into a scratch database
+   and verify row counts plus one login and one `/runs` submission
+   ([BACKUP_RESTORE.md](BACKUP_RESTORE.md), "Restore"). Record the observed
+   recovery point and wall-clock restore time against the RPO/RTO above.
+2. **Alert-path drill** — force detection end-to-end:
+   `ASSURANCE_DRILL=1 bash scripts/assurance/assurance.sh quick` must exit `90`
+   and deliver an ntfy alert ([INCIDENT.md](INCIDENT.md#alert-path-drill)).
+3. **Rollback drill** — `node scripts/run-rollback-drill.mjs` (mechanics);
+   `RUN_REAL_DRILL=1` for the live variant ([ROLLBACK.md](ROLLBACK.md)).
+
+## Evidence
+
+Append, never rewrite. For each release candidate, capture under `evidence/`:
+
+- the restore transcript and validation counts (drill 1), with the observed
+  RPO/RTO next to the targets;
+- the `exit 90` assurance ledger line and the matching `alert_log.jsonl`
+  delivery record (drill 2);
+- the rollback drill output (drill 3).
+
+Record the commit and, where relevant, the migration head with the evidence
+(`docs/EVIDENCE.md`). A release represented as *attested* must have these
+drills closed; a bounded runtime use may proceed with them recorded as open.
